<style>
    .se-success {
        background: #f7f7f7;
		border-radius: 30px;
		transition: 0.3s;
		margin-bottom: 10px;
		padding: 30px;
		text-align: center;
    }
</style>
{%- comment -%}
	This message renders inside the block's UpdatePanel after a partial postback, where inline
	<script> tags never execute. The data-scroll-to attribute is picked up by the theme's
	postback hook in Layouts/Site.Master, which scrolls the page to the selector given here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="se-success" data-scroll-to="#PageTitleContainer">
	<strong>
	Congratulations!
	</strong>
	</br>
	Your request to serve on the {{Opportunity.PublicName}} team has been submitted.
</div>